  "summary": "A flash evaporator separates vapour from a liquid by sudden pressure reduction. The liquid is heated under pressure, then throttled into a vessel at lower pressure; part of it instantly boils (\"flashes\"), cooling the rest. Vapour leaves through a demister at the top, the concentrated liquid from the bottom.",
